  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Solve each of the following equations on the given interval:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 2\\theta=1$ for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}$",
          "worked": "The sine function equals $1$ at the top of the unit circle.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\theta&\\in[0,4\\pi]\\\\2\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos 2\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for $\\theta\\in[-\\pi,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=-\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6},-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$",
          "worked": "Cosine is positive in Quadrants I and IV; the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\theta&\\in[-2\\pi,2\\pi]\\\\2\\theta&=-\\frac{5\\pi}{3},-\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=-\\frac{5\\pi}{6},-\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan 2\\theta=\\sqrt{3}$ for $\\theta\\in[0,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$",
          "worked": "Tangent is positive in Quadrants I and III; the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\theta&\\in[0,2\\pi]\\\\2\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 3\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ for $\\theta\\in[0,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{9},\\dfrac{2\\pi}{9},\\dfrac{7\\pi}{9},\\dfrac{8\\pi}{9}$",
          "worked": "Sine is positive in Quadrants I and II; the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\theta&\\in[0,3\\pi]\\\\3\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\frac{7\\pi}{3},\\frac{8\\pi}{3}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{9},\\frac{2\\pi}{9},\\frac{7\\pi}{9},\\frac{8\\pi}{9}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos 3\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$ for $\\theta\\in[0,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12},\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}$",
          "worked": "Cosine is positive in Quadrants I and IV; the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\theta&\\in[0,3\\pi]\\\\3\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{7\\pi}{4},\\frac{9\\pi}{4}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{12},\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\tan 3\\theta=-1$ for $\\theta\\in[0,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12},\\dfrac{11\\pi}{12}$",
          "worked": "Tangent is negative in Quadrants II and IV; the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\theta&\\in[0,3\\pi]\\\\3\\theta&=\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{7\\pi}{4},\\frac{11\\pi}{4}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 2\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for $\\theta\\in[-\\pi,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=-\\dfrac{11\\pi}{12},-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12},\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},\\dfrac{5\\pi}{12}$",
          "worked": "Sine is positive in Quadrants I and II; the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\theta&\\in[-2\\pi,2\\pi]\\\\2\\theta&=-\\frac{11\\pi}{6},-\\frac{7\\pi}{6},\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\\\\\theta&=-\\frac{11\\pi}{12},-\\frac{7\\pi}{12},\\frac{\\pi}{12},\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\cos 3\\theta=-1$ for $\\theta\\in[-\\pi,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=-\\pi,-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3},\\dfrac{\\pi}{3},\\pi$",
          "worked": "The cosine function equals $-1$ at the leftmost point of the unit circle.\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\theta&\\in[-3\\pi,3\\pi]\\\\3\\theta&=-3\\pi,-\\pi,\\pi,3\\pi\\\\\\theta&=-\\pi,-\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q2-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\tan 4\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $\\theta\\in[-\\pi,\\pi]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=-\\dfrac{23\\pi}{24},-\\dfrac{17\\pi}{24},-\\dfrac{11\\pi}{24},-\\dfrac{5\\pi}{24},\\dfrac{\\pi}{24},\\dfrac{7\\pi}{24},\\dfrac{13\\pi}{24},\\dfrac{19\\pi}{24}$\n\nUse reference angle $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ for $4\\theta$ and include every revolution in $[-4\\pi,4\\pi]$.",
          "worked": "Tangent is positive in Quadrants I and III; the reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Its solutions repeat every $\\pi$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4\\theta&\\in[-4\\pi,4\\pi]\\\\4\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}+k\\pi,\\qquad k=-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{24}+\\frac{k\\pi}{4},\\qquad k=-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\\\\\theta&=-\\frac{23\\pi}{24},-\\frac{17\\pi}{24},-\\frac{11\\pi}{24},-\\frac{5\\pi}{24},\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{24},\\frac{7\\pi}{24},\\frac{13\\pi}{24},\\frac{19\\pi}{24}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
